0,Nicobarese languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicobarese_languages,"The Nicobarese languages or Nicobaric languages, form an isolated group of about half a dozen closely related Austroasiatic languages, spoken by most of the inhabitants of the Nicobar Islands administered by the Indian Republic. They have a total of about 30,000 speakers.","Nicobarese, Central",Austro-Asiatic
1,"Austroasiatic languages - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",http://bluecomtech.com/Web+Sites/3D+Printer+List/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austroasiatic_languages.html,"The Austroasiatic languages, in recent classifications synonymous with Mon–Khmer, are a large language family of continental Southeast Asia, also scattered throughout India, Bangladesh, and the southern border of China.","Nicobarese, Central",Austro-Asiatic
2,"Nicobarese, Central | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ncb/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..V3G5ti537BwCzCASfxhnHe8pNlUivH5875zuS5h4fXQ,"Central Nicobarese is a stable indigenous language of India. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Nicobarese, Central",Austro-Asiatic
3,"ABVD: Nicobarese, Central",https://abvd.eva.mpg.de/austronesian/language.php?id=1197,"Language: Nicobarese, Central. Source/Author: Edward Horace Man.Classification: Austro-Asiatic:Mon-Khmer:Nicobar:Nancowry.","Nicobarese, Central",Austro-Asiatic
4,"Nicobarese, Central language resources | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/languages/ncb,"Listing of people groups speaking Nicobarese, Central. Nicobarese, Central dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.","Nicobarese, Central",Austro-Asiatic
5,Nicobarese languages,https://grokipedia.com/page/Nicobarese_languages,"The Nicobarese languages form a primary branch within the Austroasiatic language family, which comprises approximately 168 languages spoken across Mainland Southeast Asia, Northeast India, and the Nicobar Islands.","Nicobarese, Central",Austro-Asiatic
